      <h2 class="section__title">Clothing Brand Launch FAQ</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How much money do I need to start a clothing brand?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Startup costs vary significantly based on your model. Private label requires $5,000-15,000 for sampling, labels, and initial production. Custom manufacturing requires $10,000-30,000 for tech packs, pattern-making, and development. Budget additionally for website, marketing, and operations. Many founders start with $10,000-20,000 total for a focused first collection. SDF Clothing offers 300-piece minimums to keep initial production accessible. Explore <a href="/low-moq-clothing-manufacturers/">low MOQ options</a> for budget-friendly testing.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How long does it take to launch a clothing brand?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Brand launch timeline ranges from 3-6 months for private label and 6-12 months for custom manufacturing. Private label is faster because patterns and tech packs exist. Custom requires design development, pattern-making, and sampling. Factor additional time for website development, marketing preparation, and operational setup. Most realistic timelines account for potential delays in sampling or production. SDF Clothing provides detailed production schedules. Learn more about <a href="/private-label-clothing-guide">private label</a> for faster launch options.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What should I do first when starting a clothing brand?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Start by defining your brand positioning - target customer, price point, product category, and unique value proposition. Research competitors and market demand. Create mood boards and initial sketches. Simultaneously, begin researching manufacturers to understand production requirements and timelines. Strong brand foundation before production prevents costly changes later. SDF Clothing offers consultation to help founders plan their launch strategy effectively. Visit <a href="/how-to-find-clothing-manufacturer">our manufacturer guide</a> for production insights.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Do I need a business license to start a clothing brand?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Yes, you need a business license and legal structure to operate legally. Requirements vary by country and region but typically include business registration, tax identification, and potentially resale certificates for purchasing inventory. Consider trademark registration for your brand name and logo. Consult local business regulations or a legal professional to ensure compliance. Proper legal setup protects your personal assets and enables legitimate business operations. Contact <a href="/contact/">SDF Clothing</a> for production guidance.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How many pieces should I launch with?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Launch with 5-10 styles in small quantities to test market demand. Private label minimums of 300 pieces per style provide manageable inventory for testing. Focus on core products that represent your brand well rather than too many styles. Quality over quantity - fewer well-executed pieces outperform many mediocre ones. Scale successful styles in subsequent collections. SDF Clothing's flexible MOQs enable this testing approach without excessive inventory commitment. Consider <a href="/private-label-clothing-guide">private label</a> for flexible testing.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What are the most common mistakes when launching a clothing brand?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Common mistakes include launching without market research, ordering too much inventory initially, skipping samples and approving based on photos, choosing manufacturers based only on price, underpricing products, neglecting marketing preparation, inadequate legal setup, and poor operational planning. Avoid these by validating demand, starting small, reviewing physical samples, prioritizing quality over cost, pricing for profitability, building marketing assets early, establishing proper legal structure, and planning operations thoroughly. Read our <a href="/how-to-find-clothing-manufacturer">guide on finding manufacturers</a> to avoid selection mistakes.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">When should I start marketing before my clothing brand launch?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Begin marketing 2-3 months before launch. Build social media presence, collect email addresses, create content, and generate anticipation. Teaser campaigns, behind-the-scenes content, and influencer partnerships build awareness before products arrive. Marketing momentum before launch ensures day-one sales. Website should be live with coming soon page capturing leads. This pre-launch period is crucial for building audience and generating initial demand. Consider using <a href="/low-moq-clothing-manufacturers/">low MOQ options</a> to minimize risk while testing market response.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How do I find the right manufacturer for my clothing brand?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Research manufacturers specializing in your product category with relevant experience. Verify certifications like BSCI, OEKO-TEX, and ISO 9001 for quality and compliance. Request samples to evaluate construction quality. Check references from similar brands. Evaluate communication quality and responsiveness. Ensure MOQ requirements align with your budget. SDF Clothing has {companyAge} of experience serving fashion brands globally with 300-piece minimums, 13 international certifications, and comprehensive support from concept through delivery. Explore our <a href="/clothing-manufacturer-bangladesh">Bangladesh manufacturing</a> capabilities.</p>
